# Integration rules

- Vite: `generateBundle` + `enforce: 'post'`; replace CSS asset with common CSS;
  aggregate page CSS; `this.emitFile` page files.
- Next skips CSS Modules, emits hashed `static/css` chunks, wraps split common
  CSS in `@import`, and loads page CSS from page JS. `minify: false` removes
  Next's CSS minimizer.
- Vite minifies by default in production builds (`minify`); pass `minify: false`
  to opt out. Emit assets with `name` + `getFileName()` so Vite hashes them.
- Common CSS links go in HTML; page CSS is loaded from a loader prepended to
  the page JS chunk. Do not inject all page CSS links into HTML.
- Vite SPA shell: direct dynamic import chunks are pages; entry shell classes
  and CSS apply to every route. Route scans skip the entry chunk so classes do
  not leak through the shared React/runtime import. Nested dynamic chunks
  belong to their route.
- Next: only `!context.dev && !context.isServer`; hook `thisCompilation` and
  `processAssets` at `PROCESS_ASSETS_STAGE_OPTIMIZE`; use
  `compilation.updateAsset` and `compilation.emitAsset`.
- Next App Router page chunks are stubs; keep route/layout source scanning and
  relative/`@/` import traversal.
- `cssd.config.*` is loaded via jiti only when no inline options are passed.
- Never let split/report/callback failures abort the host build.
- Page chunks are emitted but not injected into HTML/manifests. State this
  limitation; use `pageUsage`/`forceCommonSelectors` for CSS Modules/dynamic
  classes.
- Run the package test and, for Next, `test:next`.
